('b1c2cd22-2fce-4027-91b9-2dbc6e129545','image',$c$WAIT OR BUY NOW? Mazda has confirmed a new generation BT-50 is coming, roughly 2028, with no price or Australian specification yet. The current ute shares its bones with the Isuzu D-Max and runs a 3.0 litre turbo diesel. Mazda is weighing a continued Isuzu diesel partnership against a link with Changan that could bring a petrol plug-in hybrid or a range extender instead. Treat the Changan route as a direction, not a done deal. A plug-in BT-50 that still tows would sit between the BYD Shark 6 and the Ford Ranger. Pictured is the current BT-50. Would you wait for it? https://www.cartell.tv/reviews/next-mazda-bt-50-confirmed-may-swap-isuzu-diesel-for-chinese-plug-in-hybrid-2026-10-06$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/cartell/1013-thu-15-oct-pm-next-mazda-bt-50.jpg'],'2026-10-15T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-cartell-2026-10-15-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Next Mazda BT-50 confirmed for about 2028. Would you wait?$a$),
