('b1c2cd22-2fce-4027-91b9-2dbc6e129545','image',$c$PRICE JUST DROPPED. The Hyundai Inster Standard Range now starts at $35,990 drive away, down $1,500, and the Inster Cross is $41,990 drive away, also down $1,500. Both offers run to 31 December 2026. The Cross claims 360 km of WLTP range. Hyundai has dropped the mid Extended Range grade after slow sales, and the five year warranty applies. A Hyundai EV under $36,000 drive away, with a known dealer network, is an easy first electric car, and it takes on the MG4 and GWM Ora. Would you buy it? https://www.cartell.tv/reviews/hyundai-inster-price-cut-35990-drive-away-2026-10-04$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/cartell/1013-fri-16-oct-pm-hyundai-inster-price-cut.jpg'],'2026-10-16T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-cartell-2026-10-16-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Hyundai Inster is $1,500 cheaper. From $35,990 drive away.$a$),
('a3361798-cb41-46cf-8545-25b50e21a6fc','image',$c$PRICE JUST DROPPED. The Hyundai Inster Standard Range now starts at $35,990 drive away, down $1,500, and the Inster Cross is $41,990 drive away, also down $1,500. Both offers run to 31 December 2026. The Cross claims 360 km of WLTP range. Hyundai has dropped the mid Extended Range grade after slow sales, and the five year warranty applies. A Hyundai EV under $36,000 drive away, with a known dealer network, is an easy first electric car, and it takes on the MG4 and GWM Ora. Would you buy it? Link in bio. #cartell #hyundai #inster #electriccars #pricedrop$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/cartell/1013-fri-16-oct-pm-hyundai-inster-price-cut.jpg'],'2026-10-16T07:32:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-cartell-2026-10-16-pm-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Hyundai Inster is $1,500 cheaper. From $35,990 drive away.$a$),
('b1c2cd22-2fce-4027-91b9-2dbc6e129545','image',$c$NEW CAR FACE-OFF. The new base Tesla Model 3 is $45,900 before on-road costs, with rear drive, 572 km of WLTP range, a glass roof and a 16 inch screen, and first deliveries are due from mid October. The Mazda 6e GT is $52,990 drive away, with 190 kW, a 78 kWh battery, up to 560 km of WLTP range and 30 to 80 per cent DC charging in about 15 minutes. Tesla quotes before on-road costs and Mazda quotes drive away, so the real gap is smaller than the $7,090 it looks. Get both quotes on the same basis. Which one would you drive? Tesla: https://www.cartell.tv/reviews/tesla-model-3-base-45900-cheapest-electric-sedan-2026-10-04 Mazda: https://www.cartell.tv/reviews/mazda-6e-now-52990-drive-away-tesla-model-3-rival-2026-09-29$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/cartell/1013-sat-17-oct-am-model-3-vs-mazda-6e-slide-1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/cartell/1013-sat-17-oct-am-model-3-vs-mazda-6e-slide-2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/cartell/1013-sat-17-oct-am-model-3-vs-mazda-6e-slide-3.jpg'],'2026-10-16T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-cartell-2026-10-17-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Tesla Model 3 at $45,900 vs Mazda 6e GT at $52,990. Not like for like.$a$),
