('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image',$c$Can you lift it? The lightest road-legal e-bike in the eBikeFinder directory is the Scott Fastlane 10 at 10.6kg. The heaviest is the Urban Arrow Family Performance cargo bike at 51kg. In between, the median folding e-bike weighs 23.0kg, the median commuter 26.0kg, the median fat tyre 35.0kg and the median cargo bike 35.8kg. The AMPD Bros Taipan is the heaviest fat tyre listed at 50kg. Weights are brand specs and bikes are ones the brand declares road-legal in Australia, so confirm both with the seller. If you carry it up stairs or onto a rack, check the kilos before you check the colour. FINDER DATA, 585 bikes compared. Method: median kg of declared road-legal bikes by directory category (road and gravel 13, folding 25, commuter 102, fat tyre 21, cargo 33 bikes), directory read 12 Oct 2026. Browse and compare: https://ebikefinder.au/ebikes Which would you rather carry up a flight of stairs? #ebikefinder$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-am-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-am-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-am-carousel-slide-3.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-am-carousel-slide-4.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-am-carousel-slide-5.jpg'],'2026-10-13T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-ebikefinder-2026-10-14-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Can you lift it? 10.6 kg to 51 kg.$a$),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image',$c$Can you lift it? The lightest road-legal e-bike in the eBikeFinder directory is the Scott Fastlane 10 at 10.6kg. The heaviest is the Urban Arrow Family Performance cargo bike at 51kg. In between, the median folding e-bike weighs 23.0kg, the median commuter 26.0kg, the median fat tyre 35.0kg and the median cargo bike 35.8kg. The AMPD Bros Taipan is the heaviest fat tyre listed at 50kg. Weights are brand specs and bikes are ones the brand declares road-legal in Australia, so confirm both with the seller. If you carry it up stairs or onto a rack, check the kilos before you check the colour. FINDER DATA, 585 bikes compared. Which would you rather carry up a flight of stairs? Link in bio. #ebike #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder #ebikeweight$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-am-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-am-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-am-carousel-slide-3.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-am-carousel-slide-4.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-am-carousel-slide-5.jpg'],'2026-10-13T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-ebikefinder-2026-10-14-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Can you lift it? 10.6 kg to 51 kg.$a$),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image',$c$Adult. Legal 250W e-bike. Footpath. New South Wales. Legal or not? Not legal. Adults cannot ride an e-bike on the footpath in NSW, whatever the bike. Riders under 16 can, and a few exemptions apply (for example medical conditions and postal workers). Victoria is the same story: 13 and older cannot ride on the footpath unless they are accompanying someone younger than 13. A compliant bike does not make the path legal. Rules differ by state, so check yours on the eBikeFinder law checker. Full state by state guide and the six question checker: https://ebikefinder.au/ebike-laws Did you get it right? Send this to someone who rides on the footpath. Not legal advice. #ebikefinder #ebikelaws$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-pm-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-pm-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ebikefinder/1013-2026-10-14-wed-pm-carousel-slide-3.jpg'],'2026-10-14T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-ebikefinder-2026-10-14-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Adult. Legal 250W e-bike. Footpath. New South Wales. Legal or not?$a$),
