('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image',$c$Gravel bike. Road bike chainstays. The Trek Checkpoint SL 7 lists a 403mm chainstay (size 56). The Giant TCR Advanced 1 road race bike lists 405mm (size M).

We pulled chainstay length from the BikeFinder Geometry Lab: 48 road bikes average 413mm and 33 gravel bikes average 432mm. Only one gravel bike is under 420mm, the Checkpoint SL 7. The next shortest is the Cervelo Aspero-5 at 422.5mm, and the longest is the Marin Four Corners 1 at 450mm.

Why it matters: a short rear end tends to make a bike quicker to flick and easier to lift over a rise. A long one steadies the bike when the tyres slide on loose ground. The Checkpoint also clears 50mm tyres, so it is a rare case of a gravel bike that keeps a road style rear end.

Method: BikeFinder Geometry Lab, chainstay field, one listed size per bike (M or 54 to 56), 81 bikes, checked 12 October 2026. Published geometry, not ride tests, and chainstay can change slightly by size. Prices last seen in AUD: Checkpoint SL 7 $6,800, TCR Advanced 1 $3,999.

Compare geometry on bikefinder.au/geometry

Would you give up stability for a lively rear end? #gravelbike #bikefinder$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/bikefinder/1013-bf-02-chainstay-lab.jpg'],'2026-10-13T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-bikefinder-2026-10-13-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Gravel bike. Road bike chainstays.$a$),
('32a573bb-697e-4c12-b64a-290a5991bbfc','image',$c$Gravel bike. Road bike chainstays. The Trek Checkpoint SL 7 has a 403mm chainstay. The Giant TCR Advanced 1 road race bike has 405mm.

We pulled the chainstay length for every bike in the BikeFinder Geometry Lab: 48 road bikes average 413mm, 33 gravel bikes average 432mm. Only one gravel bike, the Checkpoint SL 7, is under 420mm. The next shortest is 422.5mm (Cervelo Aspero-5).

Why it matters: a shorter rear end makes a bike quicker to flick and easier to lift on climbs. A longer one adds stability when the tyres are sliding. It is one reason the Checkpoint fits 50mm tyres but still feels like a road bike to some riders (our read of the numbers, not a ride test).

Method: Geometry Lab chainstay field, one listed size per bike (M or 54 to 56), 81 bikes, checked 12 Oct 2026. Chainstay can change slightly by size.

Short stays or long stays on gravel? Tell us below.

