('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image',$c$Ride2Work Day is today, Wednesday 14 October. Bicycle Network is running free bike checks and coffee at activations in Melbourne and Tasmania. If your commute bike is what is holding you back, here are four hybrids from BikeFinder, $879 to $1,400.

Merida Crossway 100, $879: Shimano CUES 9 speed, hydraulic disc brakes, 45c tyres, room for 50mm.
Trek Dual Sport 1 Gen 5, $999.99: 650b x 50mm stock tyres, the widest of the four, 8 speeds.
Giant Roam 2, $1,199: 10 speed CUES, 42c tyres, room for 53mm.
Trek FX 3 Stepover Gen 4, $1,399.99: 10 speed CUES, 35mm tyres, room for 40mm.

The pattern is tyre width. Wider tyres soak up potholes and rough paths. Narrow ones are quicker on smooth roads. Choose by your route.

Method: BikeFinder directory listings, listed AUD prices last seen and set by the retailers, checked 12 October 2026. Researched specs, not ride tests.

