('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image',$c$$5,001 for 380 grams. We compared two lightweight road bikes from the BikeFinder directory.

Specialized Aethos 2 Pro: 6.72kg listed, $12,000, Shimano Ultegra Di2 R8170, 32mm tyre clearance, 410mm chainstay (size 56).
BMC Teammachine SLR01 Four: 7.1kg listed, $6,999, Shimano Ultegra Di2, 32mm tyre clearance, 410mm chainstay (size 54).

The difference is 380g for $5,001, which works out at $13.16 per gram. The groupset family, tyre room and chainstay are the same.

Who each suits: the Aethos is for riders chasing the lightest bike for hilly racing and who value that feel. The Teammachine is for riders who want a race frame and Di2 shifting and would rather keep the five grand.

Method: listed weight and last seen AUD price from BikeFinder, sizes 56 and 54, checked 12 October 2026. Weight rises with size, so a same size comparison may differ. Researched listings, not scale tests.

Compare road bikes at bikefinder.au/type/road

Is 380g worth $5,001 to you? #roadbike #bikefinder$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/bikefinder/1013-bf-04-aethos-vs-slr01.jpg'],'2026-10-14T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-bikefinder-2026-10-14-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: $5,001 for 380 grams.$a$),
('32a573bb-697e-4c12-b64a-290a5991bbfc','image',$c$$5,001 for 380 grams. The Specialized Aethos 2 Pro lists at 6.72kg and $12,000. The BMC Teammachine SLR01 Four lists at 7.1kg and $6,999. Both run Shimano Ultegra Di2 and both clear 32mm tyres.

That is 380g lighter for $5,001 more, or $13.16 for every gram saved.

Worth it? If you race hilly events where every gram counts, maybe. If you ride for the miles, the extra five grand buys the same tyre room, the same groupset family and a very similar chainstay (410mm on both). Fit and ride feel matter more than 380g.

Method: BikeFinder directory listed weight and last seen AUD price, Aethos size 56 and BMC size 54, checked 12 Oct 2026. Weight rises with size, so the real gap at one size may differ. Researched listings, not scale tests.

