('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image',$c$Four days. 2,500m of climbing. Cape to Cape MTB starts today (15 October) in Western Australia's south west. WestCycle lists it as roughly 200km over four stages, from Cape Leeuwin to Cape Naturaliste, with stages in Nannup and Margaret River on singletrack, farm tracks, groomed downhill trails and fire trails.

Hardtail or full suspension? We checked the XC bikes in the BikeFinder directory.
Full suspension, light: Merida Ninety-Six XT, 11.8kg listed, 67 degree head angle, $7,399.
Hardtail: Superior XP 6.2, 12.9kg listed, $1,699.99. It is 1.1kg heavier and $5,700 cheaper than the Ninety-Six XT.
Budget full suspension: Scott Spark 970, 14.95kg listed, $1,899.99.
Also in our directory: Specialized Epic 8 Expert full suspension, 11.15kg listed, $11,000.
The pattern: weight tracks price more than bike type.

We do not know what the field is riding, so this is a gear guide, not a race report. Listed weights and last seen AUD prices are from BikeFinder, checked 12 October 2026. Researched specs, not ride tests.

Compare mountain bikes at bikefinder.au/type/mountain

