('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image',$c$Pidcock raced Australian wheels. At the road World Championships in Montreal, Tom Pidcock rode Partington R-Series wheels instead of his team's Zipp, and finished seventh in the elite men's road race on 27 September.

What changed: Partington says Pidcock chose the R-Series for its balance of power transfer, low weight and aerodynamics. Both versions he used have 50mm deep rims. He started on the R-Series Performance and switched to the Performance Ti (titanium hardware, titanium ratchet, ceramic bearings) after a crash with 80km to go.
The numbers: Partington claims 1,200g for the pair. Zipp claims 1,428g for the 454 NSW. Those are manufacturer claims from different sources, not an independent comparison. The Partington wheels also use carbon spokes where Zipp uses steel.
Price: The R-Series Performance is reported to retail at AUD $5,500.

This is a marketing moment, not a launch. Treat a world championship appearance as one data point, not a test.

Weights are brand claims from trade press and the price is as reported, checked 12 October 2026.

