('32a573bb-697e-4c12-b64a-290a5991bbfc','image',$c$Pidcock raced Australian wheels. At the UCI Road World Championships in Montreal, Tom Pidcock rode Partington R-Series wheels instead of his team's Zipp, and finished seventh in the elite men's road race on 27 September.

The tech: 50mm deep rims, carbon spokes, ceramic bearings on the Ti version. He started on the R-Series Performance and moved to the Performance Ti after a crash with 80km to go.
The numbers: Partington claims 1,200g a pair for the R-Series Performance. Zipp claims 1,428g for the 454 NSW he normally rides. Both are brand claims, from different sources, not an independent test.
Why we care: a local brand used at the top of the sport. Treat it as one data point, not a test result. The R-Series Performance is reported to retail at AUD $5,500.

Method: weights are brand claims from trade press, price as reported, checked 12 Oct 2026.

