('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image',$c$705g frame. 6.2kg bike. Ridley has released the all new Falcn RS on 8 October. It claims a 705g frame in a medium (the old one was 825g) and a 6.2kg complete bike in the SRAM Red AXS build.

For context: the lightest road bike in the BikeFinder directory with a listed weight is the Specialized Aethos 2 Pro at 6.72kg (size 56).

What changed: a completely new design with more traditional tube shapes, which Ridley says allow more efficient carbon layup. Frame, fork and seatpost are together claimed 12 percent lighter. Tyre clearance is 35mm, head angle 73 degrees, seat angle 76 degrees on all five sizes.
Who should care: climbers. Ridley says it is about 10 watts slower than its Noah Fast aero bike at 50km/h.
Is it better? All of this is Ridley's own claim.
Price: euro pricing only so far (Ultegra Di2 EUR 7,499, Force AXS EUR 8,499, Red AXS EUR 12,499). Ridley has not published Australian pricing, so check with a local dealer.

Method: Ridley launch coverage, BikeFinder directory weights, checked 12 October 2026.

Compare road bikes at bikefinder.au/type/road

