('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image',$c$64 degrees on a $1,500 hardtail. We pulled head angles for the mountain bikes in the BikeFinder Geometry Lab. Across 65 bikes the average is 66.8 degrees and only three are as slack as 64.0.

Marin San Quentin 1: hardtail, 130mm fork, $1,499.99.
Cannondale Habit HT 2: hardtail, 130mm fork, 1x10 Shimano CUES, $1,799.
Norco Sight A3 150: full suspension with a 160mm fork and 150mm rear travel, $3,999, and the longest reach of the three at 472.5mm in a size 3.

Why it matters: a slack front end steadies a bike on steep descents at speed. The trade is slower steering at low speed and on tight climbs. It is the enduro recipe, which makes it notable on two hardtails under $1,800.

Method: BikeFinder Geometry Lab, head angle field, one listed size per bike (mostly M, Norco size 3), checked 12 October 2026. Published geometry, not ride tests. Prices are last seen AUD listings set by the retailers.

Compare at bikefinder.au/geometry

