('32a573bb-697e-4c12-b64a-290a5991bbfc','image',$c$64 degrees on a $1,500 hardtail. We pulled the head angle for every mountain bike in the BikeFinder Geometry Lab. The average of 65 bikes is 66.8 degrees. Only three are as slack as 64.0.

1. Marin San Quentin 1: hardtail, 130mm fork, $1,499.99.
2. Cannondale Habit HT 2: hardtail, 130mm fork, $1,799.
3. Norco Sight A3 150: full suspension, 160mm fork and 150mm rear travel, $3,999.

Why it matters: a slack head angle steadies the bike on steep, fast descents. The trade is slower steering at low speed and on tight climbs. It is why enduro bikes run slack, and why it is a surprise to see it on a hardtail.

