('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image',$c$220km on Sunday. United Energy Around the Bay is on tomorrow, Sunday 18 October. Bicycle Network lists five ride options from Lap the Track to the 220km Classic around Port Phillip Bay, and 2026 is the 32nd running.

If you are riding the Classic, an endurance road bike makes sense. We compared four from the BikeFinder directory, tallest stack first:
Specialized Roubaix SL8 Pro: 605mm stack, 389mm reach, 40mm tyre clearance, 8.1kg listed, $11,900.
Trek Domane SL 5 Gen 4: 591mm stack, 377mm reach, 38mm, 9.02kg listed, $3,499.99. The most upright ratio of the four at 1.57.
Cannondale Synapse 2: 590mm stack, 387mm reach, 32mm, $2,999. The cheapest.
Giant Defy Advanced 1: 558mm stack, 380mm reach, 40mm, $4,999. The lowest of the four.

A taller stack puts you more upright, which is easier to hold for hours. More tyre room allows wider, more comfortable tyres. None of this beats a good bike fit, so ride the bike you have if it fits you.

Method: BikeFinder Geometry Lab and listings, one listed size per bike (56 or M), checked 12 October 2026. Published geometry, not ride tests. Prices are last seen AUD listings.

