('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image',$c$Same weight. SRAM or Shimano? The BMC Teammachine R 01 One lists at 7.0kg and $11,499 with SRAM Red AXS. The Merida Reacto Team lists at 7.1kg and $12,999 with Shimano Dura-Ace Di2.

Two top end race bikes, 100g apart. Tyre clearance is 30mm on the BMC and 32mm on the Merida. The Merida costs $1,500 more with a different frame, wheels and groupset, so this is a comparison of listings, not a controlled test.

Our question: if weight is no longer the difference, what decides your choice? The groupset, the frame, the wheels, the price, or the bike that fits and feels right?

Method: BikeFinder listed weight and last seen AUD price (BMC size 54, Merida size M), checked 12 October 2026. Listed weights are as published on each bike page, not scale tests.

