#ridefinder #firstride$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/ridefinder/1013-sat-2026-10-17-am-flat-tyre.jpg'],'2026-10-16T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-ridefinder-2026-10-17-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: What if you get a flat?$a$),
('5919f089-e69f-47cb-ba1b-2ee465ccb995','image',$c$What if you get a flat? Four steps, no panic.

1. Stop clear of the path and walk the bike to the side.
2. Take the wheel off and find the thorn or glass first.
3. Fit a spare tube. A patch kit is your backup.
4. Pump up, check the tyre sits evenly, refit the wheel.

Carry a spare tube, tyre levers, a pump and a multitool. Riding an e-bike with a hub motor? Practise the wheel removal at home first.

Save this for your next ride. Who needs to see it?

More guides at ridefinder.au, link in bio.
