('5919f089-e69f-47cb-ba1b-2ee465ccb995','image',$c$Small victories, then a playground. Centennial Park's Learners Cycleway in Sydney is made for first laps: allow 30 to 45 minutes, no set distance.

Mostly level, surfaced cycleway, away from the park's roads. Try a few steady starts and controlled stops, then park the bikes clear of the track and head to the playground and picnic. Check helmet fit and brakes first, and leave while there is still enthusiasm for another visit. Check gate hours and event restrictions before you go.

