('5919f089-e69f-47cb-ba1b-2ee465ccb995','image',$c$Downhill out, uphill home. Mount Evelyn station to Wandin on the Warburton Rail Trail in Victoria's Yarra Valley: about 11.2 km return, allow 1.5 to 2 hours.

Compacted trail surface, a sustained climb on the way back, so pace the first half and leave time for a picnic at the Mount Evelyn station grounds. The corridor is shared with walkers and horse riders, so slow down early and take care at road crossings. Not a flat learner circuit.

Would you take the climb home or the cafe stop first? Tell us below.

