('87db4aca-36a7-4fb1-a590-9e2a143fb42a','image',$c$Road Trip of the Week: Ikara-Flinders Ranges, South Australia. 454 km from Adelaide.

Ancient ranges, yellow-footed rock-wallabies and camping from $12.30 a night. Rangers suggest Brachina Gorge late in the afternoon for the wallabies, and Aroona or Koolamon campgrounds for early light on the Heysen Range.

Before you tow in: vehicle entry is $14.40, pets are not allowed, and most of the park closes 9pm 6 Nov to 9pm 9 Nov. Check each campground suits a caravan, and check road conditions first.

Been to the Flinders? Tell us your favourite camp. Send this to your next road trip partner.

More road trips: https://caravanscout.au/destinations

