('87db4aca-36a7-4fb1-a590-9e2a143fb42a','image',$c$Your tow limit is the lowest of five numbers.

Transport for NSW says your loaded caravan must not exceed any of these: the towbar and coupling rating, your vehicle's maximum towing capacity, the caravan's ATM, the combined mass (GCM) if your vehicle maker states one, and the tyre rating.

Their example: a car that tows 3,000 kg, a towbar rated 3,500 kg and a van with a 2,500 kg ATM. The limit is 2,500 kg.

Which number surprised you when you worked out your own? Tell us below, and send this to someone about to buy a van.

Compare weights side by side: https://caravanscout.au/compare

