('87db4aca-36a7-4fb1-a590-9e2a143fb42a','image',$c$Road Trip of the Week: Innes National Park, South Australia. 284 km from Adelaide on Yorke Peninsula.

Beaches, two operating lighthouses at Cape Spencer and West Cape, the 1904 wreck of the Ethel and plenty of kangaroos. With luck you may spot southern right whales from the cliff tops.

Before you tow in: entry is $14.40 a vehicle, camping is from $27.50 a night, dogs are not allowed, and the park had a feral bee alert on 12 Oct. The park closes on Catastrophic fire danger days.

Planning a weekend away? Tell us your favourite Yorke Peninsula stop, and send this to your travel partner.

