('e98d115c-09ce-4c5f-bf24-4c5d3df31147','image',$c$What exactly is koji?

A mould, grown on purpose. Aspergillus oryzae is grown on steamed rice or other grain, and its enzymes break starch into sugars and protein into amino acids. That second part is where a lot of umami comes from.

It is behind miso, soy sauce and sake, and chefs now use it on meat and vegetables too.

Have you ever ordered koji on purpose? Tell us below.

