('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$One pram, two weights. Mountain Buggy's nano urban is listed at 6 kg with its travel wheels and 7.3 kg with its urban wheels. Both figures include the frame, seat, canopy, wheels, gear tray and grab bar. It folds to 30 x 53 x 52 cm with the travel wheels on. The same page also shows 7.6 kg in its summary table, so check which wheels a weight is quoted for. Which would you carry more often, the stairs or the kerb? Compare prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-am-nano-urban-two-weights.jpg'],'2026-10-12T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-13-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: One pram, two weights.$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$One pram, two weights. Mountain Buggy's nano urban is listed at 6 kg with its travel wheels and 7.3 kg with its urban wheels. Both figures include the frame, seat, canopy, wheels, gear tray and grab bar. It folds to 30 x 53 x 52 cm with the travel wheels on. Always check which wheels the weight is quoted for. Which would you carry more often, the stairs or the kerb? Link in bio. #pramkin #pramsaustralia #strollerreview #newparents$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-am-nano-urban-two-weights.jpg'],'2026-10-12T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-13-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: One pram, two weights.$a$),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$Small boot? Compare the fold, not the weight. Folded sizes as the makers list them, worked out in litres: Baby Jogger city tour 2 about 56 L (59.5 x 49.5 x 19 cm), Nuna SWIV about 106 L (37 x 54 x 53 cm), Nuna TRVL lx about 152 L (40 x 52 x 73 cm), Edwards & Co Oscar Nu about 272 L (65 x 53 x 79 cm, frame folded with wheels on). Litres are our arithmetic from the listed size, and none of these has been tested in a car by Pramkin, so the car fit label is no evidence yet. Measure your boot, then compare. Which would you rather lift in? Compare up to three prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-3.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-4.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-5.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-6.jpg'],'2026-10-13T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-13-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Small boot? Compare the fold, not the weight.$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$Small boot? Compare the fold, not the weight. Folded sizes as the makers list them, worked out in litres: Baby Jogger city tour 2 about 56 L (59.5 x 49.5 x 19 cm), Nuna SWIV about 106 L (37 x 54 x 53 cm), Nuna TRVL lx about 152 L (40 x 52 x 73 cm), Edwards & Co Oscar Nu about 272 L (65 x 53 x 79 cm, frame folded with wheels on). Litres are our arithmetic from the listed size, and none of these has been tested in a car by Pramkin, so the car fit label is no evidence yet. Measure your boot, then compare. Which would you rather lift in? Link in bio. #pramkin #pramsaustralia #smallcar #newparents #strollerreview$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-3.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-4.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-5.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-13-pm-fold-litres-6.jpg'],'2026-10-13T07:32:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-13-pm-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Small boot? Compare the fold, not the weight.$a$),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$Bassinet on, new fold. Bugaboo Cub folds to 55 x 60 x 87 cm with the seat and 60 x 60 x 95 cm with the bassinet, so the newborn setup is 5 cm longer and 8 cm taller. Bugaboo Dragonfly goes the other way: 36 x 52 x 90 cm with the seat, 32 x 52 x 90 cm with the bassinet. Weights: Cub 10.7 kg with seat, 11 kg with bassinet. Dragonfly 9.9 kg with seat, 10.5 kg with bassinet. Check the fold for the setup you will use in the first six months. Which setup are you planning for? Compare prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-am-bassinet-fold.jpg'],'2026-10-13T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-14-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Bassinet on, new fold.$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$Bassinet on, new fold. Bugaboo Cub folds to 55 x 60 x 87 cm with the seat and 60 x 60 x 95 cm with the bassinet, so the newborn setup is 5 cm longer and 8 cm taller. Bugaboo Dragonfly goes the other way: 36 x 52 x 90 cm with the seat, 32 x 52 x 90 cm with the bassinet. Weights: Cub 10.7 kg with seat, 11 kg with bassinet. Dragonfly 9.9 kg with seat, 10.5 kg with bassinet. Check the fold for the setup you will use in the first six months. Which setup are you planning for? Link in bio. #pramkin #newbornessentials #pramsaustralia #newparents$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-am-bassinet-fold.jpg'],'2026-10-13T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-14-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Bassinet on, new fold.$a$),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$Planning for a second child? Check what is in the box on day one. Cybex Gazelle S takes two seats (2 x 22 kg) but ships with one seat unit, 12.9 kg, folds to 32 x 56 x 74.5 cm. Bugaboo Kangaroo is $1,999, was $2,049, 13.05 kg with seat, folds to 50 x 62 x 97 cm. UPPAbaby Vista V3 is $1,799 with bassinet, 12.5 kg for frame and seat, folds to 41.4 x 65.3 x 85.9 cm, and extra seats or a board for a second or third child. Nuna TRVL dubl is two seats from day one, 11.5 kg, folds to 41 x 78 x 74 cm. None has been car tested by Pramkin, so car fit is no evidence yet. Which one would your hallway handle? Compare up to three at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-3.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-4.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-5.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-6.jpg'],'2026-10-14T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-14-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Planning for a second child?$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$Planning for a second child? Check what is in the box on day one. Cybex Gazelle S takes two seats (2 x 22 kg) but ships with one seat unit, 12.9 kg, folds to 32 x 56 x 74.5 cm. Bugaboo Kangaroo is $1,999, was $2,049, 13.05 kg with seat, folds to 50 x 62 x 97 cm. UPPAbaby Vista V3 is $1,799 with bassinet, 12.5 kg for frame and seat, folds to 41.4 x 65.3 x 85.9 cm, and extra seats or a board for a second or third child. Nuna TRVL dubl is two seats from day one, 11.5 kg, folds to 41 x 78 x 74 cm. None has been car tested by Pramkin, so car fit is no evidence yet. Which one would your hallway handle? Link in bio. #pramkin #pramsaustralia #secondbaby #newparents #strollerreview$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-3.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-4.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-5.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-14-pm-growing-family-6.jpg'],'2026-10-14T07:32:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-14-pm-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Planning for a second child?$a$),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$How much can the basket carry? Underseat basket maximum loads as the makers list them: Bugaboo Donkey 6 15 kg or 70 L, UPPAbaby Vista V3 13.6 kg, Bugaboo Dragonfly 10 kg, Baby Jogger city tour 2 7 kg, Baby Jogger city mini GT3 4.5 kg plus a 1 kg seat pocket. Check the listed basket load, not just the look of it, before you plan the weekly shop around a pram. What is the heaviest thing you have ever wedged under a pram? Compare prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-15-am-basket-loads.jpg'],'2026-10-14T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-15-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: How much can the basket carry?$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$How much can the basket carry? Underseat basket maximum loads as the makers list them: Bugaboo Donkey 6 15 kg or 70 L, UPPAbaby Vista V3 13.6 kg, Bugaboo Dragonfly 10 kg, Baby Jogger city tour 2 7 kg, Baby Jogger city mini GT3 4.5 kg plus a 1 kg seat pocket. Check the listed basket load, not just the look of it, before you plan the weekly shop around a pram. What is the heaviest thing you have ever wedged under a pram? Link in bio. #pramkin #pramsaustralia #newparents #strollerreview$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-15-am-basket-loads.jpg'],'2026-10-14T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-15-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: How much can the basket carry?$a$),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$A frame is not a whole pram. Cybex Priam and Mios 3 frames list the frame, hard seat unit, basket, bumper bar, rain cover and car seat adaptors in the box, and the seat pack and carry cot are sold separately (Priam frame 12.9 kg, folds to 31.5 x 51.5 x 85 cm. Mios frame 9.8 kg, folds to 30 x 50 x 65 cm). The iCandy Core 2 is $1,499 at iCandy Australia with the chassis, seat unit, capsule adaptors, elevator adaptors and rain cover in the box list, and the 3.7 kg carrycot is not on that list. Price the whole setup before you compare. What was the extra you did not plan for? Compare prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-15-pm-whats-in-the-box-1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-15-pm-whats-in-the-box-2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-15-pm-whats-in-the-box-3.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-15-pm-whats-in-the-box-4.jpg'],'2026-10-15T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-15-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: A frame, not a pram$a$),
