('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$Price watch: Valcobaby Snap Ultra Series2 is listed at $649 on Valcobaby Australia, and the Snap Ultra Elite is on sale at $669, down from $739 ($70 off). Series2 has a reversible seat, one-hand fold and comes in Basil, Cocoa and Pitch. Sale prices change, so check the current price and the spec sheet for each before you choose. Series2 or Elite? Compare prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-16-am-price-watch-valco.jpg'],'2026-10-15T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-16-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Snap Ultra: $649 or $669?$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$Price watch: Valcobaby Snap Ultra Series2 is listed at $649 on Valcobaby Australia, and the Snap Ultra Elite is on sale at $669, down from $739 ($70 off). Series2 has a reversible seat, one-hand fold and comes in Basil, Cocoa and Pitch. Sale prices change, so check the current price and the spec sheet for each before you choose. Series2 or Elite? Link in bio. #pramkin #pricewatch #pramsaustralia #newparents$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-16-am-price-watch-valco.jpg'],'2026-10-15T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-16-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Snap Ultra: $649 or $669?$a$),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$Car seat adaptors: in the box or extra? Nuna TRVL takes the Nuna KLIK plus capsule with no adaptors (capsule sold separately). Cybex Priam and Mios 3 frames list car seat adaptors in the box. iCandy Core 2 lists capsule adaptors in the box. Bugaboo lists Dragonfly Maxi-Cosi adapters as a separate accessory. Always check which capsule model fits your pram before you buy either one. Which capsule are you planning to use? Compare prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-16-pm-capsule-adaptors.jpg'],'2026-10-16T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-16-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Car seat adaptors: in the box or extra?$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$Car seat adaptors: in the box or extra? Nuna TRVL takes the Nuna KLIK plus capsule with no adaptors (capsule sold separately). Cybex Priam and Mios 3 frames list car seat adaptors in the box. iCandy Core 2 lists capsule adaptors in the box. Bugaboo lists Dragonfly Maxi-Cosi adapters as a separate accessory. Always check which capsule model fits your pram before you buy either one. Which capsule are you planning to use? Link in bio. #pramkin #travelsystem #pramsaustralia #newparents$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-16-pm-capsule-adaptors.jpg'],'2026-10-16T07:32:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-16-pm-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Car seat adaptors: in the box or extra?$a$),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$Top weight for the child: how long will it last? Maximum child weight as the makers list it: Baby Jogger city mini GT3 29.5 kg, iCandy Core 2 25 kg, Nuna SWIV 22.7 kg, UPPAbaby Vista V3 22.7 kg, Cybex Mios 3 22 kg, Baby Jogger city tour 2 20.5 kg. That is a weight limit, not an age, so check the maker's age guidance and newborn setup too. Does your toddler get a say in the next pram? Compare prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-17-am-max-child-weight.jpg'],'2026-10-16T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-17-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Top weight for the child.$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$Top weight for the child: how long will it last? Maximum child weight as the makers list it: Baby Jogger city mini GT3 29.5 kg, iCandy Core 2 25 kg, Nuna SWIV 22.7 kg, UPPAbaby Vista V3 22.7 kg, Cybex Mios 3 22 kg, Baby Jogger city tour 2 20.5 kg. That is a weight limit, not an age, so check the maker's age guidance and newborn setup too. Does your toddler get a say in the next pram? Link in bio. #pramkin #pramsaustralia #toddler #newparents$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-17-am-max-child-weight.jpg'],'2026-10-16T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-17-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Top weight for the child.$a$),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$Can the fabrics go in the wash? Silver Cross says the Cove 2 outer fabrics and carrycot cover come off and wash at 30°C. Bugaboo says the Donkey 6 fabrics are machine washable at 30°C, with the basket and leather look grips wiped with a damp cloth. Cybex says the Mios fabric covers are machine washable at 30°C. Always follow the care label on your own pram. What is the worst mess a pram has survived at your place? Compare prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-17-pm-wash-day.jpg'],'2026-10-17T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-17-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Can the fabrics go in the wash?$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$Can the fabrics go in the wash? Silver Cross says the Cove 2 outer fabrics and carrycot cover come off and wash at 30°C. Bugaboo says the Donkey 6 fabrics are machine washable at 30°C, with the basket and leather look grips wiped with a damp cloth. Cybex says the Mios fabric covers are machine washable at 30°C. Always follow the care label on your own pram. What is the worst mess a pram has survived at your place? Link in bio. #pramkin #pramcare #newparents #pramsaustralia$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-17-pm-wash-day.jpg'],'2026-10-17T07:32:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-17-pm-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Can the fabrics go in the wash?$a$),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$Cruz or Vista? One child or more? $500 and 8 cm apart. UPPAbaby Cruz V3 is $1,299, 12 kg with seat, folds to 57.2 cm wide (seat attached), takes one child and has the infant insert in the box. Vista V3 is $1,799, 12.5 kg, folds to 65.3 cm wide, takes up to three children with extra seats or a board, and has a bassinet in the box. UPPAbaby says choose Cruz when one child is the plan or boot space matters more. Which are you? Compare prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-18-am-cruz-or-vista.jpg'],'2026-10-17T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-18-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Cruz or Vista? $500 and 8 cm.$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$Cruz or Vista? One child or more? $500 and 8 cm apart. UPPAbaby Cruz V3 is $1,299, 12 kg with seat, folds to 57.2 cm wide (seat attached), takes one child and has the infant insert in the box. Vista V3 is $1,799, 12.5 kg, folds to 65.3 cm wide, takes up to three children with extra seats or a board, and has a bassinet in the box. UPPAbaby says choose Cruz when one child is the plan or boot space matters more. Which are you? Link in bio. #pramkin #uppababy #pramsaustralia #newparents$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-18-am-cruz-or-vista.jpg'],'2026-10-17T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-18-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Cruz or Vista? $500 and 8 cm.$a$),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image',$c$What $649 to $1,999 buys, with one fact from each maker's page. Valcobaby Snap Ultra Series2 $649, reversible seat and one-hand fold. UPPAbaby Minu V3 $749, 7.6 kg and ready from birth as sold. UPPAbaby Cruz V3 $1,299, infant insert in the box. iCandy Core 2 $1,499, seat unit in the box, no carrycot on the box list. UPPAbaby Vista V3 $1,799, bassinet in the box. Bugaboo Kangaroo $1,999, was $2,049, 13.05 kg with seat. Prices change, so check before you buy. Where does your budget land? Compare prams at pramkin.com.au #pramkin$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-18-pm-price-ladder.jpg'],'2026-10-18T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-18-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: What $649 to $1,999 buys.$a$),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image',$c$What $649 to $1,999 buys, with one fact from each maker's page. Valcobaby Snap Ultra Series2 $649, reversible seat and one-hand fold. UPPAbaby Minu V3 $749, 7.6 kg and ready from birth as sold. UPPAbaby Cruz V3 $1,299, infant insert in the box. iCandy Core 2 $1,499, seat unit in the box, no carrycot on the box list. UPPAbaby Vista V3 $1,799, bassinet in the box. Bugaboo Kangaroo $1,999, was $2,049, 13.05 kg with seat. Prices change, so check before you buy. Where does your budget land? Link in bio. #pramkin #pricewatch #pramsaustralia #newparents$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/pramkin/1013-2026-10-18-pm-price-ladder.jpg'],'2026-10-18T07:32:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-pramkin-2026-10-18-pm-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: What $649 to $1,999 buys.$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$BMW M4 for ages 2 to 5. The licensed BMW M4 Competition 12V from Little Tacker Toys is a single seater with a 12V 7Ah battery, two 35W motors, a 30kg max load and a top speed of up to 8km/h. It has a parent remote, two speed modes, a seatbelt, opening doors and push start sounds. $329 in black or blue, $339 in silver (price and stock checked 12 Oct 2026). Run time is listed at 1 to 1.5 hours and a full charge at 8 to 10 hours, both claimed by the retailer. Compare it with 48 other ride-ons at tinywhips.com.au. Would you pick black or silver? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-01-tue-am-bmw-m4.jpg'],'2026-10-12T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-13-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: BMW M4 for ages 2 to 5: a licensed 12V with a parent remote, from $329$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$A drift kart for the driveway. The Little Tacker Toys 24V DriftX is a single seater for ages 3 to 8 with two motors, a 13km/h top speed, a drift button and a frame that lengthens up to 130cm. Max load is 50kg combined. It comes with a parent remote, seatbelt, front safety bar and LED lights, and the retailer lists 60 to 90 minutes of run time and an 8 to 10 hour charge. Swipe for the details. EVA foam front tyres and drifting rear tyres suit flat, hard surfaces, and the retailer makes no grass claims. $459 in red, yellow, white or pink, $469 in painted grey (price and stock checked 12 Oct 2026). More kids' ride-ons compared at tinywhips.com.au. Which surface would it be driven on at your place? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-02-tue-pm-s1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-02-tue-pm-s2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-02-tue-pm-s3.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-02-tue-pm-s4.jpg'],'2026-10-13T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-13-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: A drift kart for the driveway: the 24V DriftX, ages 3 to 8, $459$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$The priciest whip we track: $2,800. The Peg Perego Gaucho Superpower 24V is a two seater for ages 6+ with a 24V 12Ah sealed lead acid battery, two 340W motors and a 60kg combined max load. Kids Car Sales and Yardgames both list it at $2,800 (checked 12 Oct 2026). Kids Car Sales shows it available, Yardgames shows it out of stock. The next dearest of the 49 ride-ons in our directory is the Peg Perego Corral T-Rex quad at $1,080, so this one is a long way clear. Specs and prices for every ride-on, dated, at tinywhips.com.au. Is $2,800 ever worth it for a ride-on? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-03-wed-am-gaucho-price.jpg'],'2026-10-13T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-14-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: The priciest whip we track: the Peg Perego Gaucho Superpower 24V, $2,800$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$6V, 12V or 24V? What the volts mean. 6V ride-ons are first rides for toddlers on smooth, flat ground. 12V is the common one, suited to preschoolers on flat ground and short lawn. 24V is for older kids, two riders and rougher ground. Across the 49 Australian listings in our directory, 6V covers 8 whips (listed max load 20 to 30kg), 12V covers 23 whips (25 to 60kg) and 24V covers 18 whips (30 to 100kg). Voltage is not a speed rating, so read the motors, wheels and max load as well. The full guide is at tinywhips.com.au/guides/6v-vs-12v-vs-24v. Which voltage are you shopping for? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-04-wed-pm-volts-guide.jpg'],'2026-10-14T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-14-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: 6V, 12V or 24V? What the volts mean for your kid and your yard$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$A quad for grass and gravel. The Little Tacker Toys 24V Off Road Hero ATV has a 24V 7Ah battery, twin silent motors, a carbon steel frame and a 100kg load capacity. Rear shock absorbers and silent EVA tyres are listed for backyards, grass, gravel and uneven ground. It has high and low speed modes, reverse, a braking function and Bluetooth music. No parent remote is listed, and the retailer says helmets must be worn. $429 in white or green (price and stock checked 12 Oct 2026). Swipe for the details, then compare it with 48 other ride-ons at tinywhips.com.au. What surface does your yard throw at a quad? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-05-thu-am-s1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-05-thu-am-s2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-05-thu-am-s3.jpg'],'2026-10-14T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-15-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: A quad for grass and gravel: the Little Tacker 24V Off Road Hero, $429$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$Same kart, $33 apart. The Rollplay Flex Kart 6V is $109 at Kmart (online only, sold by Klika Group) and $141.99 at Toys"R"Us, both checked 12 Oct 2026. It has a foldable frame, a 6V rechargeable battery, a top speed of up to 3km/h and a 25kg max load. It weighs 6.35kg and is listed at 83 x 28.5 x 25.5cm. One catch: the spec sheet says 4+ years but Kmart tags it for ages 5 to 7, so check with the seller before you buy. Prices move, so we date them. Every ride-on, side by side, at tinywhips.com.au. Is a foldable kart a good fit for your place? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-06-thu-pm-s1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-06-thu-pm-s2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-06-thu-pm-s3.jpg'],'2026-10-15T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-15-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Same Rollplay Flex Kart 6V, $33 apart: Kmart $109, Toys"R"Us $141.99$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$Weekend pick: a Lamborghini for ages 3 to 7. The Kahuna Lamborghini Performante 12V is a single seater with a 12V 4.5Ah battery, two 25W motors and a 28kg max load. It has a parent remote with a listed range of up to 30 metres, a seatbelt, swing open doors with a safety lock, working lights and a horn, EVA wheels and a USB and MP3 input. $367 at Kids Car Sales (price and stock checked 12 Oct 2026). The retailer does not publish a top speed or run time, so we do not either. Every ride-on, with dated prices, at tinywhips.com.au. Would your driver pick yellow? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-07-fri-am-lamborghini.jpg'],'2026-10-15T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-16-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Weekend pick: the licensed Kahuna Lamborghini Performante 12V for ages 3 to 7, $367$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$A 4WD quad under $300. The MC Wholesalers 12V electric quad bike (pink) is a single seater for ages 3+ with a 12V 7Ah battery, four motors and 4WD, a recommended load of about 35kg and a listed top speed of 4 to 6km/h. It has a 2.4G parent remote, a safety belt, LED headlights and plastic tyres the retailer calls suitable for backyard and driveway use. Run time is listed at 60 to 90 minutes. $299 at MC Wholesalers (price and stock checked 12 Oct 2026), also sold in red and white. Adult supervision is required. See how it stacks up at tinywhips.com.au. Pink, red or white? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-08-fri-pm-quad-under-300.jpg'],'2026-10-16T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-16-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: A 4WD quad under $300: the 12V MC Wholesalers pink quad, $299$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$A drift kart for bigger kids. The Little Riders 24V Go Kart Rambler is for ages 8+ and has two 250W motors, a 24V 10Ah battery, a top speed of up to 13km/h, a 70kg max load and a lap sash seatbelt. It comes with solid drift wheels, which the retailer calls a consumable that can wear. A helmet that meets Australian Standards must be worn. It is $399 (was $449) as a pre-order from Little Riders, arriving 16 Nov 2026, so it is one for the Christmas list now (checked 12 Oct 2026). Compare it with every other ride-on for older kids at tinywhips.com.au. What age would you hand over the keys? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-09-sat-am-rambler.jpg'],'2026-10-16T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-17-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: A drift kart for bigger kids: the Little Riders 24V Rambler, ages 8+, $399 pre-order$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$Licensed or look-alike? Read the badge. A licensed ride-on carries the real brand's name, badges and styling under an agreement with the car maker. That does not mean the car maker designed, tested or certified it, because a toy maker builds it. Some listings borrow a real car name for a vehicle that is only styled to look similar, and where a listing does not clearly say officially licensed, we do not mark it as licensed. Compare licensed and non-licensed models on the same specs: max load, voltage, motors, wheels, remote, parts and warranty. The full guide is at tinywhips.com.au/guides/licensed-vs-non-licensed-ride-ons. Does the badge matter to your driver? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-10-sat-pm-licensed-guide.jpg'],'2026-10-17T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-17-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Licensed or look-alike? What the badge on a ride-on does and does not tell you$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$Sunday pick: a tractor with a front loader and a trailer. The POSHO 24V Farm Tractor is for ages 3+ with a 24V 7Ah battery, two 200W motors and a 60kg load capacity. It has a front digger, a removable trailer, a rooftop canopy, a safety belt, working headlights and a 2.4G parent remote as well as manual drive. $475 (was $540) as a pre-order from POSHO, with the ETA listed as end of October (price checked 12 Oct 2026). Pick up is in store, and the page shows Laverton North VIC as in stock, meaning on the way. See it against every other ride-on tractor at tinywhips.com.au. Who is on yard duty at your place? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-11-sun-am-posho-tractor.jpg'],'2026-10-17T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-18-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Sunday pick: the POSHO 24V farm tractor with front loader and trailer, $475 pre-order$a$),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image',$c$Not sure which whip? Answer ten quick questions. The Whip Finder at tinywhips.com.au asks about your child's age, weight, how many riders, the surface they will drive on, whether you want a parent remote and your budget, then narrows the 49 ride-ons in our directory. Skip any question you are unsure about, and every result explains why it matched. Specs are sourced and prices are dated, with no paid rankings. Take the quiz at tinywhips.com.au/finder. What is your biggest question before you buy? #tinywhips$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/tinywhips/1013-post-12-sun-pm-whip-finder.jpg'],'2026-10-18T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-tinywhips-2026-10-18-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Not sure which whip? Answer ten questions with the Whip Finder quiz$a$),
('dfe6d125-63b5-46f6-abf4-9b69d29375ad','image',$c$250 km in Adelaide. What does it cost? A petrol car using 7.0 L/100km burns 17.5 litres a week. At the $2.35/L Adelaide average the ACCC reported for 7 October, that is $41. An EV using 16 kWh/100km needs 40 kWh. Charged at home on the SA Power Networks flat rate default market offer (41.9c/kWh, the highest of the flat rates in the AER's 2026/27 tables), that is $17. About $24 back every week, even on the highest flat rate in those tables. Your car and your plan will move those numbers. What do you pay per kWh at home? #evibe #evcharging$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p01-tue-am.jpg'],'2026-10-12T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-13-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: 250 km in Adelaide. What does it cost?$a$),
('3e927b65-717a-45f9-9284-4faed0091d8e','image',$c$250 km in Adelaide. What does it cost? Petrol at 7.0 L/100km and $2.35/L: $41. EV at 16 kWh/100km charged at home at 41.9c/kWh: $17. About $24 back every week. Assumptions are on the tile. Send this to someone with a long commute. Link in bio. #evibe #evcharging #electricvehicles #evaustralia #fuelprices$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p01-tue-am.jpg'],'2026-10-12T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-13-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: 250 km in Adelaide. What does it cost?$a$),
('dfe6d125-63b5-46f6-abf4-9b69d29375ad','image',$c$Free power, 11am to 2pm daily. Victoria's Midday Power Saver started on 1 October 2026. Households with a smart meter can ask their retailer for a regulated plan with free electricity from 11am to 2pm every day. It is opt in, so nobody is switched automatically. The state estimates $149 to $428 a year saved if you shift 5 to 30% of your use into the free window. The catch: the government says prices outside those hours rise a little, and if you cannot shift your use you may pay more than on another plan. In the Powercor zone the maximum peak rate (4pm to 9pm) is 43.81c per kWh. A 7 kW home charger running for the three hours puts about 21 kWh into a car, roughly 130 km at 16 kWh per 100 km, which is $9.20 at that peak cap. Other zones differ. This is general information, so check your own usage first. Do you charge at midday? #evibe #evcharging$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p02-tue-pm.jpg'],'2026-10-13T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-13-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Free power, 11am to 2pm daily.$a$),
('3e927b65-717a-45f9-9284-4faed0091d8e','image',$c$Free power, 11am to 2pm daily. Victoria's Midday Power Saver started 1 October. Smart meter and opt in needed. State estimate: $149 to $428 a year if you shift 5 to 30% of your use. Catch: rates outside the window rise a little. A 7 kW charger for three hours is about 21 kWh, roughly 130 km, worth $9.20 at the 43.81c Powercor peak cap. Send this to a Victorian with an EV. Link in bio. #evibe #evcharging #middaypowersaver #victoria #energybills$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p02-tue-pm.jpg'],'2026-10-13T07:32:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-13-pm-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Free power, 11am to 2pm daily.$a$),
('dfe6d125-63b5-46f6-abf4-9b69d29375ad','image',$c$14,000 public chargers. Your cost: $1 a year. On 24 September the Australian Energy Market Commission released a draft rule to support the Commonwealth's $40 million Accelerating EV Charging Program, which aims to place about 14,000 chargers in regional blackspots and high density areas where people have little off street parking. The Commonwealth funds about 30% of eligible infrastructure and participating networks recover the other 70% from electricity customers. The AEMC estimates that adds about $1 a year to a typical household bill for five years. It is a draft, not final: submissions close on 5 November 2026 and a final decision is due by the end of the year. Some retailers and industry groups have objected, so the rule could change. Would you pay $1 a year for more chargers? #evibe #evcharging$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p03-wed-am.jpg'],'2026-10-13T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-14-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: 14,000 public chargers. Your cost: $1 a year.$a$),
('3e927b65-717a-45f9-9284-4faed0091d8e','image',$c$14,000 public chargers. Your cost: $1 a year. Draft rule released 24 September: Commonwealth funds about 30%, networks recover the other 70% from bills, about $1 a year for a typical home over five years (AEMC estimate). Submissions close 5 November. Still a draft. Send this to someone who rents or lives in an apartment. Link in bio. #evibe #evcharging #electricvehicles #evaustralia #publiccharging$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p03-wed-am.jpg'],'2026-10-13T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-14-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: 14,000 public chargers. Your cost: $1 a year.$a$),
('dfe6d125-63b5-46f6-abf4-9b69d29375ad','image',$c$153 batteries for every 100 solar systems. The Clean Energy Council's Rooftop Solar and Storage Report for January to June 2026 counts 276,011 home batteries installed against 180,878 rooftop solar systems. In the second half of 2025 the ratio was 130 batteries per 100 systems. The batteries added 8,691 MWh of storage, more than double the 4,221 MWh of the half before. If you already have solar and are weighing a battery, get quotes that state the install date and the rebate you will receive, because the Cheaper Home Batteries discount steps down on 1 January. Do you have a battery yet? #evibe #homebattery$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p04-wed-pm.jpg'],'2026-10-14T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-14-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: 153 batteries for every 100 solar systems.$a$),
('3e927b65-717a-45f9-9284-4faed0091d8e','image',$c$153 batteries for every 100 solar systems. Jan to Jun 2026: 276,011 home batteries installed, 180,878 rooftop solar systems (Clean Energy Council). It was 130 per 100 in the second half of 2025. 8,691 MWh of storage added. Send this to someone with solar and no battery. Link in bio. #evibe #homebattery #solarbattery #rooftopsolar #energybills$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p04-wed-pm.jpg'],'2026-10-14T07:32:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-14-pm-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: 153 batteries for every 100 solar systems.$a$),
('dfe6d125-63b5-46f6-abf4-9b69d29375ad','image',$c$3.095c a km is coming. Still ahead by $1,000. NSW has legislated a distance based road user charge for eligible EVs. It starts on 1 July 2027, or when EVs reach 30% of new vehicle sales if that comes first, and the 2026-27 rate is 3.095 cents per km for a battery EV (2.476 cents for a plug-in hybrid), indexed to CPI each year. Nobody is being billed yet. Here is the maths for a Sydney driver doing 12,000 km a year. Petrol car at 7.0 L/100km: 840 litres at $2.39 (ACCC, 7 October) is $2,008. EV at 16 kWh/100km on the Ausgrid flat rate default offer (33.1c/kWh): 1,920 kWh is $636, plus the charge of $371, so $1,008. About $1,000 a year still saved, before service costs. NSW says it is still assessing what the High Court's 2023 Vanderstock decision means for its charge, so the details could change. Would a per km charge change what you buy? #evibe #evcharging$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p05-thu-am.jpg'],'2026-10-14T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-15-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: 3.095c a km is coming. Still ahead by $1,000.$a$),
('3e927b65-717a-45f9-9284-4faed0091d8e','image',$c$3.095c a km is coming. Still ahead by $1,000. NSW EV road user charge: from 1 July 2027 or at 30% of new sales, 3.095c per km for a battery EV in 2026-27, indexed. Sydney, 12,000 km a year. Petrol 7.0 L/100km at $2.39: $2,008. EV 16 kWh/100km at 33.1c plus the charge: $636 + $371 = $1,008. About $1,000 saved. Not billed yet. Send this to someone weighing an EV in NSW. Link in bio. #evibe #evcharging #electricvehicles #nsw #roaduser$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p05-thu-am.jpg'],'2026-10-14T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-15-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: 3.095c a km is coming. Still ahead by $1,000.$a$),
('dfe6d125-63b5-46f6-abf4-9b69d29375ad','image',$c$Same 4,600 kWh. $616 apart. The AER's final 2026/27 default market offer caps the flat rate residential bill for 4,600 kWh a year at $1,988 in the Energex area (south east Queensland) and $2,604 in the Essential Energy area (regional NSW), GST included. Spread over the usage, that is 43.2c per kWh all in versus 56.6c. South Australia is the one region of the five where the flat rate cap rose: up $33 to $2,334 for 4,000 kWh. These are caps for default offers, not every plan on the market, so your bill depends on your retailer and your usage. Do you know your all in cost per kWh? #evibe #energybills$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p06-thu-pm.jpg'],'2026-10-15T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-15-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Same 4,600 kWh. $616 apart.$a$),
('3e927b65-717a-45f9-9284-4faed0091d8e','image',$c$Same 4,600 kWh. $616 apart. Default offer cap 2026/27, flat rate, GST incl: Energex (SE QLD) $1,988, Essential Energy (regional NSW) $2,604. All in that is 43.2c vs 56.6c per kWh. SA is the only one of the five regions where the cap rose (+$33 to $2,334). A cap on default offers, not every plan. Send this to someone who pays a lot for power. Link in bio. #evibe #energybills #electricitybill #solarpower #australia$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p06-thu-pm.jpg'],'2026-10-15T07:32:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-15-pm-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Same 4,600 kWh. $616 apart.$a$),
('dfe6d125-63b5-46f6-abf4-9b69d29375ad','image',$c$Petrol is 68c a litre dearer than February. The ACCC's weekly report (published 9 October) puts the five city average at $2.39 a litre for petrol and $2.81 for diesel on 7 October. Compared with pre conflict levels on 20 February, that is 68c more for petrol and 104c more for diesel. A 50 litre petrol fill is $119.50 now against about $85.50 then, roughly $34 more. An 80 litre diesel fill is $224.80 against about $141.60, roughly $83 more. For comparison, 100 km in a 7.0 L/100km petrol car costs $16.73 at $2.39, while an EV using 16 kWh/100km charged at home on the Ausgrid flat rate default offer (33.1c/kWh) costs $5.30. Your car and tariff will move those numbers. What did your last fill cost? #evibe #fuelprices$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p07-fri-am-s1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p07-fri-am-s2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p07-fri-am-s3.jpg'],'2026-10-15T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-16-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Petrol is 68c a litre dearer than February.$a$),
('3e927b65-717a-45f9-9284-4faed0091d8e','image',$c$Petrol is 68c a litre dearer than February. ACCC, 7 Oct: petrol $2.39, diesel $2.81 (five city average). A 50 L petrol fill: $119.50 vs about $85.50 in February. An 80 L diesel fill: $224.80 vs about $141.60. 100 km by plug at home: $5.30 vs $16.73 petrol. Assumptions on the slides. Send this to someone at the bowser. Link in bio. #evibe #fuelprices #electricvehicles #evaustralia #energybills$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p07-fri-am-s1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p07-fri-am-s2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p07-fri-am-s3.jpg'],'2026-10-15T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-16-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Petrol is 68c a litre dearer than February.$a$),
('dfe6d125-63b5-46f6-abf4-9b69d29375ad','image',$c$Myth tested: "Time of use is always cheaper." Verdict: only by a little on the default offer. In the AER's final 2026/27 default market offer, the time of use bill for an average household is just $6 to $74 a year below the flat rate bill: Ausgrid $1,893 versus $1,899, Endeavour $2,320 versus $2,328, SA Power Networks $2,276 versus $2,334, and Energex and Essential Energy $74 less each. The catch is the evening peak, for example 47.79c per kWh from 4pm to 9pm at Energex. Time of use pays when you move big loads such as EV charging or the dishwasher out of the peak. Do you know which tariff you are on? #evibe #energybills$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p08-fri-pm.jpg'],'2026-10-16T07:30:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-16-pm-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Is time of use cheaper? Barely.$a$),
('3e927b65-717a-45f9-9284-4faed0091d8e','image',$c$Myth tested: "Time of use is always cheaper." Verdict: only a little. Default offer 2026/27, average household: time of use is $6 to $74 a year below flat. Energex and Essential $74, Ausgrid $6. Peak is 47.79c from 4pm to 9pm at Energex. It pays if you move your use. Send this to someone on time of use. Link in bio. #evibe #energybills #electricityplan #timeofuse #australia$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p08-fri-pm.jpg'],'2026-10-16T07:32:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-16-pm-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: Is time of use cheaper? Barely.$a$),
('dfe6d125-63b5-46f6-abf4-9b69d29375ad','image',$c$One kWh costs 33c. It moves an EV 6 km. On the Ausgrid flat rate default offer (33.1c per kWh), an EV using 16 kWh per 100 km covers about 6 km on one kWh. A 7.0 L/100km petrol car needs 0.44 litres for the same 6 km, which is $1.05 at the $2.39 five city average the ACCC reported for 7 October. Same 33c, different job: a heat pump with an efficiency of about 3 puts roughly 3 kWh of heat into a room from 1 kWh of power, so 3 kWh of heat costs about 33c against 99c from a resistive heater. Your number is on your bill: the flat rate default offer caps are 28.0c per kWh in Energex (south east Queensland), 33.1c in Ausgrid (Sydney) and 41.9c in SA Power Networks (Adelaide). What do you pay per kWh? #evibe #energybills$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p09-sat-am-s1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p09-sat-am-s2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p09-sat-am-s3.jpg'],'2026-10-16T22:00:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-17-am-facebook',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: One kWh costs 33c. It moves an EV 6 km.$a$),
('3e927b65-717a-45f9-9284-4faed0091d8e','image',$c$One kWh costs 33c. It moves an EV 6 km. Petrol for the same 6 km: $1.05. A heat pump (efficiency about 3) gives 3 kWh of heat for 33c, a resistive heater 99c. Flat rate default offer caps 2026/27: Energex 28.0c, Ausgrid 33.1c, SA Power Networks 41.9c per kWh. What is yours? Send this to someone who has not read their bill. Link in bio. #evibe #energybills #heatpump #electricvehicles #australia$c$,ARRAY['https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p09-sat-am-s1.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p09-sat-am-s2.jpg','https://raw.githubusercontent.com/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media/15da38d/posts/2026-10-13/evibe/1013-p09-sat-am-s3.jpg'],'2026-10-16T22:02:00+00','queued','roxy','r1013-evibe-2026-10-17-am-instagram',$a$Roxy preflight 12 Oct: full size contact sheet audit of every slide, sources per manifest (verified 12 Oct), white bg, no dashes, no repeat of 2026-09-28/10-05 manifests. Hook: One kWh costs 33c. It moves an EV 6 km.$a$)
